<title>USA: U.S. seeks best bids Nov 7 in SPR sale third round.</title>
<headline>U.S. seeks best bids Nov 7 in SPR sale third round.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. government called for best and final offers Thursday at 1300 EST/1800 GMT in the third round of its ongoing oil sale from the Strategic Petroleum Reserve, a government official said Monday.</p>
<p>Awards, if any, will be announced later on November 7.</p>
<p>The Clinton administration is in the process of selling sour crude from the emergency stockpile to raise $220 million to cover the costs of running the oil reserve.</p>
<p>In the first two rounds of the auction, which began two weeks ago, the government raised $72.6 million.</p>
</text>
